Track 3: Hala-Jouvert
- Story & Context: In the colossal, humid cathedral of Chamber 9—an abandoned extraction vault where condensation tastes of battery acid and iron shavings—thousands of off-shift miners gather in secret beneath the border of two closed mine fields for the annual dawn blowout. The band fired up four diesel generators, sending twin twenty-foot exhaust flues into sustained acoustic overdrive while steel drums tuned to microtonal minor triads drove the crowd into a manic, synchronized stomping frenzy. By the time surface inspectors reached the hatch at sunrise, the tunnel was deserted except for an automatic pneumatic drill clattering against an oil drum in an unbroken loop, echoing the final chant painted across the rock: "The border ends where the hammer hits the pan!"
